  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EF Gender Chapter FTM TJNA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The GET FTM project is structured around a co-creation effort for developing and refining the GET FTM methodology with extensive participation from EF&#x2019;s staff and relying in its in-house expertise.
After the draft GET FTM methodology and the scoresheet have been developed by ON and TJN-A, both documents will be shared with EF (and any other organizations selected by EF to join this stage of the project). Once EF has the draft GET FTM methodology, it will perform an initial review of the documents and provide broad feedback on the overall structure of the proposed methodology, identify potential gaps, propose changes to current questions and new questions it considers helpful towards achieving the overarching objectives of the GET project.
All input andfeedback provided by EF will be reviewed by ON and TJN-A, with exchange of e-mails and conference calls taking place until a final version of the GET FTM methodology and the scoresheet have been agreed upon by all parties. The final version of both documents will be the central pillars of theGET FTM project.
Once the documents are finalized, they will be shared with the local partner organizations so all staff involved in the common training sessions can take a first look at the material in advance of the training.</narrative>
  </description>
